{{- if !listed && p.use == "lifecycle" && p.bound_attribute }}

## Lifecycle

The attribute {{ md_code (p.subject.name + "." + p.bound_attribute.name) }} of {{ md_code p.subject.name }} holds the top-level state{{ if p.bound_enum }}, as a member of the enum {{ md_code p.bound_enum.name }}{{ end }}; a nested state counts as its top-level ancestor.

| State | Enum member |
| --- | --- |
{{- for s in p.bound_states }}
| {{ md_code s.path }} | {{ s.bound_member ? (md_code s.bound_member.name) : "none" }} |
{{- end }}
{{- else if listed }}

## Lifecycle
{{- if p.subjects.size > 0 }}

| Subject | Attribute | Type |
| --- | --- | --- |
{{- for sj in p.subjects }}
| {{ md_code subject_label(p, sj) }} | {{ sj.bound_attribute ? (md_code (subject_label(p, sj) + "." + sj.bound_attribute.name)) : "none" }} | {{ if !sj.bound_attribute }}{{ else if sj.bound_enum }}enum {{ md_code sj.bound_enum.name }}{{ else if sj.bound_reference_type }}reference type {{ md_code sj.bound_reference_type.name }}{{ else }}{{ md_code attr_type(sj.bound_attribute) }}{{ end }} |
{{- end }}
{{- end }}
{{- if coded.size > 0 }}

{{ if p.codes_map }}The codes form a map: an attribute bound to a reference type or a plain status holds the code of the state's nearest coded ancestor, and a state with none has no code.{{ else }}The codes do not form a map, since two coded states share a path or one sits inside a parallel region: they are constants only, and no attribute can hold them.{{ end }}

| State | Code |
| --- | --- |
{{- for s in coded }}
| {{ md_code s.path }} | {{ md_code (json s.code) }} |
{{- end }}
{{- end }}
{{- if p.bound_enum }}

The attribute {{ md_code (p.subject.name + "." + p.bound_attribute.name) }} holds the top-level state as a member of the enum {{ md_code p.bound_enum.name }}.

| State | Enum member |
| --- | --- |
{{- for s in p.bound_states }}
| {{ md_code s.path }} | {{ s.bound_member ? (md_code s.bound_member.name) : "none" }} |
{{- end }}
{{- end }}
{{- end }}
{{- if pack.params.diagrams && p.all_states.size > 0 }}

